direction: right
design: DEV physical restoration admission
source: Frozen source span
grant: Accepted destination interval
copy: Copy exactly A+F words
marker: Canonical first-break eligibility revocation
restore: Publish restored / collective join
context: Reacquire and reload execution context
whole: Original stress-GSI whole acceptance OPEN {style.fill: "#fff4cc"}
history: Repair9 references only {style.fill: "#dbeafe"}
history -> design: falsifiers, no inherited pass
design -> grant: same epoch and held lifetime
source -> copy
grant -> copy
copy -> marker: destinationFirstBreak=D-F
marker -> restore: active words preserved
restore -> context
context -> whole: qualified producer and unchanged workload
lifetime: Section retirement {style.fill: "#fff4cc"}
predecessor: Logical predecessor
readers: Stack and heap interval owners / old readers
reuse: Reissue physical section
focused: Native p2 map / wide roots PASS
tfib: Compiled p2 TFIB failed {style.fill: "#fee2e2"}
design -> lifetime
predecessor -> lifetime: frame recovery edge
readers -> lifetime: exclusive grant and reader drain required
lifetime -> reuse: only after retirement
context -> focused
context -> tfib
tfib -> whole: coordinate correction insufficient
claim: Private claim per semispace
park: Park stack with its floor
payload: Carrier reuse list outside Scheme payload
design -> claim
claim -> park
park -> predecessor
lifetime -> claim: retire old parity only after GC drain
reuse -> payload

rest: Rest batch and GC retry {
  preflight: Rest or keyword-rest full batch preflight
  fast: Accepted batch on current interval
  source: Partial rest and original argument window
  bank: Typed RC roots published
  mapped: ACK and mapped retry frame
  repaired: GC repairs root span
  reserve: Reload and reserve in current epoch
  ready: Initialized vector then READY
  claim: One claim and processed-argument tail entry
  preflight -> fast: interval fits
  preflight -> source: refused before first fallback store
  source -> bank: retain original custody
  bank -> bank: lost reply queries same attempt
  bank -> mapped: complete root installation
  mapped -> repaired
  repaired -> reserve
  reserve -> mapped: refusal with roots retained
  reserve -> ready: complete batch fits
  ready -> claim: transfer roots to final arguments
}
context -> rest.preflight
rest.claim -> whole: exact-image controls plus unchanged original run

rest_record: Rest activation record lifetime {
  token: VM incarnation, slot, generation
  pin: Validate and pin before first record read
  close: Close lookup admission
  drain: Drain last reader and settle receipts
  recycle: Retire or reuse with new generation
  token -> pin
  close -> pin: refuse new pins
  close -> drain -> recycle
  pin -> drain: existing pin delays release
}
rest.source -> rest_record.token: refusal opens an attempt
rest_record.pin -> rest.bank: install precise roots under RC authority
rest_record.pin -> rest.reserve: re-resolve before reading repaired slots
rest.claim -> rest_record.close: consumed or explicitly abandoned

candidate_rest: Current generated handler cut {style.fill: "#fff4cc"}
scheme_observer: DEV Scheme body and ordered trace oracle
candidate_rest -> rest.preflight: handler 7 and handler 9
candidate_rest -> rest.mapped: complete frame missing before GC
rest.claim -> scheme_observer: same attempt and one body entry
scheme_observer -> whole: same GSI receipt required

construction: Family 6 construction gates {
  producer: Bind source, generated frame ABI and GSI
  record: Lifetime before first read
  frame: Complete retry frame and exact RC roots
  round: Frozen origin, moving repair, current interval
  delivery: One claim, real tail entry and Scheme body
  attribution: First violation, wait cycle or completed work
  original: Original p2 then p1 under 295 / 300 seconds
  producer -> record -> frame -> round -> delivery -> attribution -> original
}
construction.frame -> rest.mapped: generated map and install ACK
construction.round -> rest.reserve: repaired slots and new grant
construction.original -> whole: independent family verdict
